@startuml
title Move Enemies

hide footbox

legend top right
  |<#E6E6E6> View (React / TypeScript) |
  |<#CFE3F7> Controller (Java) |
  |<#D8F0D8> Model (Java) |
endlegend
autonumber

skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor LightCyan
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor DarkSlateGray
skinparam ActorBackgroundColor White
skinparam ActorBorderColor DarkSlateGray
skinparam ArrowColor SlateGray
skinparam SequenceLifeLineBorderColor SlateGray
skinparam SequenceGroupBorderColor DarkSlateGray
skinparam DefaultFontName Arial
skinparam note {
    BackgroundColor LightYellow
    BorderColor Orange
}

' ==========================================
' Participants, coloured by MVC layer as in "Explode Bomb" (see legend).
' Player and Enemy both extend the abstract class Creature (pixel
' position, sub-pixel counter, hitbox, centerCell(), isFullyInside(),
' isAlive(), die()). An enemy's die() also returns its base points.
' Each Enemy has an EnemyType (speed, direction-timer range, points,
' wall pass) and a MovementStrategy (Strategy pattern):
'   RandomWalk     - Ballom
'   AxisChaser     - Onil (column), Dall (row), Minvo and Kondoria (both)
'   Alternating    - Ovapi
'   JunctionWalker - Parse
'   Pursuer        - Pontan
' Speed tiers, in px per tick (Bomberman: 0.75): slowest 0.375
' (Kondoria), slow 0.5 (Ballom, Ovapi), medium 0.75 (Onil, Dall),
' fast 1.0 (Minvo, Parse, Pontan). Constants, to be tuned by eye.
' ==========================================
actor "Time" as time

participant "GameLoop" as view #E6E6E6

participant "GameBridge" as bridge #CFE3F7

participant "game : Game" as game #D8F0D8
participant "stage : Stage" as stage #D8F0D8
participant "enemy : Enemy" as enemy #D8F0D8
participant "strategy : MovementStrategy" as strategy #D8F0D8
participant "explosion : Explosion" as explosion #D8F0D8

time -> view : next animation frame
view -> bridge : tick(inputMask)
bridge -> game : update(input)
game -> stage : update(input)

note over stage, explosion
  Everything below runs within one tick (1/60 s), as the third part of
  stage.update(): 1. the player ("Move Bomberman", "Place Bomb",
  "Detonate Bomb Remotely"), 2. bombs ("Explode Bomb"), 3. the stage
  timer ("Run Out of Stage Time"), then enemies (this diagram). Enemies pass through each other,
  so they never check one another. Touching the player is checked in
  "Move Bomberman" on the next tick.
end note

loop for each living enemy
    stage -> enemy : move(this)
    note right of stage : this = Stage as Arena\n(same interface as for the player).

    enemy -> enemy : step = pixels for this tick
    note right of enemy
      Its type's speed; the sub-pixel counter
      carries the remainder, as for the player.
      Types with a timer also count it down here.
    end note

    ' ==========================================
    ' 1. Choosing a direction (only at a cell's center)
    ' ==========================================
    opt enemy is at the center of a cell
        enemy -> strategy : chooseDirection(enemy, arena)
        note right of strategy
          MovementStrategy is an interface. The enemy does
          not know which strategy it has; the alt below shows
          what each implementation does.
        end note

        alt RandomWalk (Ballom)
            opt direction timer ran out
                strategy -> strategy : direction = random passable direction
                strategy -> enemy : resetTimer()
            end
        else AxisChaser (Onil, Dall, Minvo, Kondoria)
            strategy -> stage : lookForPlayer(enemy)
            stage --> strategy : direction to the player, or NONE
            alt player seen along one of its axes
                strategy -> strategy : direction = toward the player
                note right of strategy : Does not reset\nthe timer.
            else direction timer ran out
                strategy -> strategy : direction = random passable direction
                strategy -> enemy : resetTimer()
            end
        else Alternating (Ovapi)
            opt direction timer ran out
                strategy -> stage : playerCell()
                stage --> strategy : cell
                strategy -> strategy : direction = toward the player, or\naway from him (alternates each time)
                strategy -> enemy : resetTimer()
            end
        else JunctionWalker (Parse, no timer)
            strategy -> stage : lookForPlayer(enemy)
            stage --> strategy : direction to the player, or NONE
            alt player seen
                strategy -> strategy : direction = toward the player
            else at a junction
                strategy -> strategy : direction = random passable direction
            end
        else Pursuer (Pontan, no timer)
            strategy -> stage : playerCell()
            stage --> strategy : cell
            strategy -> strategy : direction = the passable direction\nthat brings it closest to the player
        end
        strategy --> enemy : direction
    end

    note over stage, strategy
      lookForPlayer: the player is alive and in the same row or column,
      with nothing between that this enemy could not walk through
      (hard blocks, bombs, and soft blocks unless it has wall pass).
      An enemy sees along any line it could also walk.
    end note

    ' ==========================================
    ' 2. Moving along the lane
    ' ==========================================
    enemy -> stage : isPassable(next cell in direction, enemy)
    stage --> enemy : passable
    note right of stage
      Same rules as for the player (see "Move
      Bomberman"): bombs block (except one it still
      overlaps), soft blocks unless the type has wall
      pass. Lingering flames do not block.
    end note

    alt passable
        enemy -> enemy : position += step in direction
    else blocked by a hard block, a soft block or a bomb
        enemy -> strategy : onBlocked(enemy, arena)
        strategy --> enemy : new direction
        enemy -> enemy : resetTimer()
        note right of enemy
          At a cell's center it may take any passable
          direction; between two cells it can only
          turn around. Pontan and Parse simply pick
          again by their own rule. If no direction is
          passable at all (boxed in by bombs and blocks),
          the enemy waits in place until one opens.
        end note
    end
    enemy --> stage

    ' ==========================================
    ' 3. Walking into a lingering flame
    ' ==========================================
    loop for each explosion
        stage -> explosion : burns(enemy.centerCell())
        explosion --> stage : burning
        opt burning and enemy still alive
            stage -> enemy : die()
            enemy --> stage : basePoints
            stage -> explosion : scoreKill(basePoints)
            explosion --> stage : points
            stage -> game : onEnemyKilled(points)
        end
    end
end

note over stage, explosion
  A killed enemy plays its death animation and is then removed
  from the stage. It no longer counts as living, so it cannot
  touch the player, and noEnemiesLeft() ignores it.
end note

stage --> game
game --> bridge
bridge --> view
note over view, bridge : The frame is then drawn as in\n"Explode Bomb" (getState, draw, sounds).

@enduml
